{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109472-how-do-you-do-that-give-extra-temporary-health-levels-to-a-vampire","id":1109472,"title":"How do you do that - Give extra temporary health levels to a vampire?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-29T16:35:52-07:00","id":1109472,"title":"How do you do that - Give extra temporary health levels to a vampire?","content":"If you wanted to give extra health levels to a vampire how would you do that? Which level of Matter do you employ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T18:53:30-07:00","id":1109533,"title":"","content":"I'd say you'd need both Matter and Life to accomplish this. Life 4 to transform another's pattern, and Matter 4 to transmute the dead flesh into that which does not really exist: Healthier dead flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T23:38:05-07:00","id":1109639,"title":"","content":"There is also the possibility to do that with Prime 4 as per HDYDT","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T00:17:53-07:00","id":1109644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109472-how-do-you-do-that-give-extra-temporary-health-levels-to-a-vampire?p=1109639#post1109639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the possibility to do that with Prime 4 as per HDYDT</div> </div> </div> </div>You would still have to slap matter onto it, just like how you would have to add spirit if you did it to a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T01:17:11-07:00","id":1109657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109472-how-do-you-do-that-give-extra-temporary-health-levels-to-a-vampire?p=1109644#post1109644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You would still have to slap matter onto it, just like how you would have to add spirit if you did it to a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is support in RAW, that Prime doesn't need other spheres to affect things:<br /> <br /> With Prime 5 you can annihilate every pattern be it human, undead, garou or inanimate(for this Prime 4 is sufficient).<br /> <br /> I don't see why you suddenly have to use conjunctional Matter to infuse a Vampire pattern with quint and therefore give HL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T04:59:07-07:00","id":1109700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109472-how-do-you-do-that-give-extra-temporary-health-levels-to-a-vampire?p=1109657#post1109657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is support in RAW, that Prime doesn't need other spheres to affect things:<br /> <br /> With Prime 5 you can annihilate every pattern be it human, undead, garou or inanimate(for this Prime 4 is sufficient).<br /> <br /> I don't see why you suddenly have to use conjunctional Matter to infuse a Vampire pattern with quint and therefore give HL.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sphere synergy has always been a thing alluded to in all the Mage books, so it's very much up for interpretation.<br /> High level spheres tend to have the ability to affect things that could be in the realm of other spheres. Entropy 4 for Life, Mind 4 for Spirit, Time 4 for Entropy, Matter 5 for Forces, etc. Because of this I tend to say that there should never be redundancy in spheres. Even if similar effects are possible with the same spheres, they will always be some kind of difference either in outcome or in process.<br /> <br /> Entropy 4 can influence the outcome of a life pattern, but not how it gets there, while Life 4 can influence the life pattern directly, consequences rising out of whatever changes are made. Using both will allow the mage full control on both how the life pattern develops, and where it ends up.<br /> <br /> This is supported by the Astral Sojourn rote. While Mind 4 is enough to visit the Astral Realm, bypassing the storm, and Spirit 3 is enough to visit the penumbra via the storm. Both together (with a bit of prime) allows you to go to the penumbra bypassing the storm and travel the Astral Realm as unhindered as you would with just Mind.<br /> <br /> Therefore, you could very easily make the argument that Prime 4 is sufficient for giving a vampire quintessence. But then I'd say if you happened to have Matter as well, it would work better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 06-30-2017, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T06:13:46-07:00","id":1109722,"title":"","content":"As Saikou said, and by working better our group usually represents this by requiring less successes for the effect, or shorter ritual times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T07:13:17-07:00","id":1109747,"title":"","content":"Just sew some blood bags into them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T08:53:09-07:00","id":1109783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Saikou said, and by working better our group usually represents this by requiring less successes for the effect, or shorter ritual times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed<br /> <br /> However, in this case, because Prime it's very different than Life, I would accept Prime alone working as well for vampires as it would for a human...but for a human it may work better with Life 3-4 (because the added knowledge may help to reinforce the Pattern in the correct places, creating a better support), and for a vampire you could be able to do it with Prime alone or, better, with Prime + Life and Matter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T07:41:55-07:00","id":1110541,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd say Entropy rather than Life + Matter. extrapolating from the rote Slay Machine/Perfect Function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T17:14:11-07:00","id":1110696,"title":"","content":"Quintessence = Blood Points, which vampires can use to restore their own health levels, so I'd be inclined to let Prime 4 suffice as long as you weren't trying to make physical alterations to the vampire's body. More just like supercharging the vitae in their system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}